Notebook[{
Cell["\<\
When does the photon come back? Jaynes-Cummings with dissipation\
\>", "Title",
 CellID->874461601,ExpressionUUID->"22a1a762-10e3-861e-525e-3f4ca097ed64"],

Cell["\<\
A single two-level atom sits inside a cavity that holds one electromagnetic \
mode. The atom can give its excitation to the field as a photon and take it \
back again, and in a closed cavity this exchange is a clean oscillation: the \
Rabi oscillation. Real cavities are not closed. The atom can decay into modes \
outside the cavity, and the cavity mirror leaks photons to the outside world. \
Both losses drain the excitation that the oscillation is passing back and \
forth.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->36768919,ExpressionUUID->"4da796ef-9f57-a4bf-7b5c-0fc91ae30e85"],

Cell["\<\
So the question is: with both channels open, what happens to the exchange? \
Two things, and this example computes both. First, an atom that starts high \
up the ladder, with several photons already in the cavity, shows a Rabi \
oscillation under a decaying envelope: the exchange keeps going while the \
excitation slowly bleeds away. Second, an atom that starts with a single \
quantum, so that only one photon can ever be in play, splits into three \
regimes set by how the coupling compares with the loss rates: the excitation \
either oscillates under decay, or stops oscillating at a critical ratio, or \
never oscillates at all and the atom simply decays faster than it would in \
free space.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1699946459,ExpressionUUID->"1b39f900-6440-cee7-4ac6-f16a0dfa94cd"],

Cell["The model: two loss channels draining one exchange", "Section",
 CellID->1535504786,ExpressionUUID->"75d93363-5da6-51a4-23e6-ab4d5453238e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Let ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    StyleBox["e", "TI"]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25a568a6-87a2-527f-535a-810032572145"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    StyleBox["g", "TI"]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "00d7f70d-8d0e-ae34-30ec-ef5724b8f51e"],
 " be the excited and ground atomic states, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2f3e8453-9762-68ea-56c5-1e1d22173a30"],
 " the cavity Fock states with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5902d484-617f-9570-0f31-cdee100bfc5a"],
 " photons. The atom is the first subsystem and the field the second. The \
atomic operators are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["g", "TI"]},
     "Ket"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["e", "TI"]},
     "Bra"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "56e0e12c-de7d-6135-7e9f-f889db08301f"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "+"], "=", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-", "\[Dagger]"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5708d032-2150-04f2-7d37-ca7c50e56ed8"],
 ", and the field operator obeys ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]},
     "Ket"]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    SqrtBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]], 
    TemplateBox[{
      RowBox[{
        StyleBox["n", "TI"], "-", "1"}]},
     "Ket"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b7807e8-9504-b25a-6907-9eb21cb600a0"],
 ". In the rotating-wave approximation the Jaynes-Cummings Hamiltonian is"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1208482393,ExpressionUUID->"166f8969-5e31-e8e5-3e14-21335bc5bacf"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\[HBar]", 
      StyleBox["\[Nu]", "TI"], 
      SuperscriptBox[
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"]}], "+", 
     RowBox[{
      FractionBox["1", "2"], "\[HBar]", 
      StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
      SubscriptBox[
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
       StyleBox["z", "TI"]]}], "+", 
     RowBox[{"\[HBar]", 
      StyleBox["g", "TI"], 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          OverscriptBox[
           StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-"], 
         SuperscriptBox[
          OverscriptBox[
           StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"]}], "+", 
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          OverscriptBox[
           StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "+"], 
         OverscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"]}]}], ")"}]}]}]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      TemplateBox[{
        StyleBox["e", "TI"]},
       "Ket"], 
      TemplateBox[{
        StyleBox["e", "TI"]},
       "Bra"]}], "-", 
     RowBox[{
      TemplateBox[{
        StyleBox["g", "TI"]},
       "Ket"], 
      RowBox[{
       TemplateBox[{
         StyleBox["g", "TI"]},
        "Bra"], "."}]}]}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->28909615,ExpressionUUID->"234f1fb7-07c6-bba9-5174-96f1b27009f3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The interaction turns ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    RowBox[{
      StyleBox["e", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ee45b93-a0df-d1f6-169c-52dcd16ba3dc"],
 " into ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    RowBox[{
      StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1"}]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0a3edd72-e0d3-62fb-3bc5-d53f916630c1"],
 " and back, so it conserves the total number of excitations ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "+", 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "+"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ec9a758-58be-624c-16f6-3f02594b3096"],
 ". In other words, every photon the field gains is a quantum the atom has \
lost, and that sum stays fixed under the coupling. We take the resonant case ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Nu]", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "23253b8d-1c99-a6bf-52da-b2d7952d0c85"],
 ". On resonance the two states ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    RowBox[{
      StyleBox["e", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e84829b-9667-6594-16bb-1bc523124ffe"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    RowBox[{
      StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1"}]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "569e173f-6b36-b240-7ea5-8f790ec000aa"],
 " that the coupling mixes carry the same free energy, so the first two terms \
contribute only an overall phase to each excitation manifold and the \
excited-state population is set entirely by the coupling and the losses."
}], "Text",
 CellID->193832008,ExpressionUUID->"15a3e88e-0b57-fa6e-4350-01e8aee3c8b4"],

Cell["\<\
Dissipation enters through a Lindblad master equation with two jump \
operators, atomic decay and cavity photon loss,\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->684317082,ExpressionUUID->"779c57de-bb93-d239-1da4-4e983e27a103"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "^"]}], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], "=", "-", 
    FractionBox[
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[HBar]"], 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "^"]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "+", "\|01d49f", 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["L", "TI"], "^"], "1"], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "^"], "+", "\|01d49f", 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["L", "TI"], "^"], "2"], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "^"]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["L", "TI"], "^"], "1"], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     SqrtBox[
      StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-"], "\[CircleTimes]", 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["I", "TI"], "^"]}]}]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["L", "TI"], "^"], "2"], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     SqrtBox[
      StyleBox["\[Kappa]", "TI"]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     RowBox[{
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["I", "TI"], "^"], "\[CircleTimes]", 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"]}]}]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->528485616,ExpressionUUID->"2867ea9b-6e8d-517b-581c-03c50b382041"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\|01d49f", 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["L", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "^"], "=", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["L", "TI"], "^"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "^"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["L", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], "-", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["L", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["L", "TI"], "^"], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "^"], "+", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "^"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["L", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["L", "TI"], "^"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "76dfbc62-92ac-7b6e-1ee4-364c275949b4"],
 ". Here ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0df4b6a5-173c-e15a-3b8b-2f0fa2ceb3a0"],
 " is the atomic decay rate and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Kappa]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4d620fc7-5cf2-d9d8-7b11-a6a15484ab22"],
 " the cavity photon-loss rate. The atomic jump ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "741b091d-feb2-1a39-1c38-a146fb476903"],
 " lowers the atom without touching the field; the cavity jump ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3bf5a20e-c541-e06e-698a-446becf5b2b4"],
 " removes a photon without touching the atom."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1392207227,ExpressionUUID->"07964fa7-8d1e-ff14-2dae-660124a8c27e"],

